course: dictionary
lesson: 9631
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives several meanings for studio, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Foley artists make everyday sounds in a studio and match them to the film.» Here a studio is a place where sounds are made and recorded, because the sentence is about films.
explain: Read the words around the word. In «She moved into a studio flat near the park», the words flat and moved tell you it is a small home with one main room. In «The painter spent all morning in her studio», the word painter tells you a studio is a room where an artist works.
explain: Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Studio is a noun: a studio, two studios.
fact: A studio is a room where an artist, photographer or dancer works.
fact: A studio is a place where films, TV or radio programmes or music are made and recorded.
fact: A studio flat is a small home with one main room for living and sleeping.
fact: A film company can be called a studio, as in «Aardman is a British studio.»
exercise: In «Wallace and Gromit are made by the British studio Aardman», what does studio mean? | A painter's room | A small home with one main room | *A film company | A dance hall
exercise: «She moved into a studio flat near the park.» What does studio mean here? | A place where TV is recorded | A film company | *A small home with one main room | A room where a painter works
exercise: «The painter spent all morning in her studio, mixing colours.» Which word tells you the studio is a room where an artist works? | mixing | colours | *painter | morning
test: «The dancers practised in the studio every Tuesday.» What does studio mean here? | A TV set with cameras | *A room where a dancer works | A film company | A small home for one person
test: «The recording studio was full of singers and microphones.» Which meaning fits? | A room where a painter works | A studio flat | A film company | *A place where music is recorded
exam: «The studio was packed for the live show, with cameras and lights everywhere.» Which meaning fits? | A small home for one person | A room where an artist works | *A place where TV programmes are made | A studio flat
